Z||000000||NASAReeves||05-12-2001||06:39 PM||||One more question.  While inspecting my plenum, I have discovered a small hole/chip in my plenum, near the throttle body.  It is not near the edge...oddly enough, it is in the middle of nowhere.  Anybody have any ideas as far as patching/filling this hole?  I don't know if it goes all the way through the plenum (it is close to the Holly), but I do see shiny silver, and no doubt...it is a hole. It is small in size...maybe 1/8" in diameter.<P>Thanks again, everybody!||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||05-12-2001||06:47 PM||||Nasa, I found the very same thing.  I don't think the hole was all the way through, but I filled it with epoxy anyway,  Dave||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||05-12-2001||07:13 PM||||When GM drilled the holes for the throttle body screws they drilled too far on one andas a result there is a small hole on the plenum.  It does absolutely nothing and should be covered by the plug wires (if they are properly routed). ||||reg||1
